# Frontend craft — measurable rules

These are checked by `scripts/dev/layout_audit.mjs`. A change is not done until the audit passes on every surface that shares the primitive you touched.

## Spacing
- One scale: `--space-1..8` (4/8/12/16/24/32/48/64). No literal px for margin, padding, or gap. `0` is allowed.
- A container's padding is symmetric unless a rule below says otherwise. Bars (`.hub-page-sticky`, toolbars, table headers) have equal top and bottom padding; children carry no vertical margin inside a bar.
- Vertical rhythm between page sections is one token (`--inset-section`). Hero → gap → content. Never 0 between two containers, never two different gaps on one page.
- Text never touches text. Every heading/paragraph pair has a margin from the scale. Two inline text runs on one line are separated by ` · ` or a gap token, never by nothing. Collision checks compare block-level siblings only — inline children of one paragraph (a leftover number in `<strong>`) are supposed to sit adjacent.
- Disclosures, footnotes, and "see also" lines live inside the card they refer to, not floating between cards.

## Alignment
- Every horizontal group (bar, row, toolbar, button pair) is `align-items: center` and all its controls share one height token (`--control-h-sm` 32 / `--control-h-md` 40 / `--control-h-lg` 44). No mixed heights in one row.
- Segmented controls and tabs center their labels. Fixed-width segments center; content-width segments use equal horizontal padding.
- Tables: numeric columns (`$`, points, ranks, counts, deltas) right-align the cell AND the header. Text columns left-align both. Never center a column unless it is a single glyph (Pos, injury mark). The action column right-aligns.
- Table column widths: first text column takes the remainder; numeric columns are `min-content` + padding. No column may be wider than 1.5× its widest cell unless it is the remainder column. The same pack and align rules apply to `table`, `[role=table]`, `[role=grid]`, and CSS-grid row groups.
- Content in a card/table fills the card. No dead zone > `--space-6` on either side of a table inside its card.
- Page containers share one max-width and one horizontal inset. Hero band, strip, and main cards start at the same x. The summary rail is the right column — do not compare its left edge to the hero.

## Grids and wrapping
- Card grids use `repeat(auto-fill, minmax(<token>, 1fr))`, never a fixed column count. An orphan row is acceptable only if it's the last row of an auto-fill grid. Layout grids (hero beside a rail) may have unequal heights — the audit only checks auto-fill / auto-fit card grids.
- Cards in one auto-fill grid share one height: pin the action to the bottom (`margin-top: auto`), clamp titles to 2 lines with ellipsis, reserve the action slot even when empty.
- Text that wraps differently per card (badge, meta line) gets a fixed line count or a fixed height. Never let a badge push a sibling's timestamp onto two lines.

## Controls
- Interactive targets are ≥ 32 tall at 1280 and ≥ 44 at 390. Do not apply the phone 44 floor on desktop. Lock/Skip/Add/History in a row share one style tier (all buttons or all links, not mixed).
- One primary per viewport. A second blue filled button on screen is a bug. Undo, secondary, and "browse" are ghost or text. Do not demote whichever `.btn-primary` is second in the DOM to satisfy the audit — each extra primary is a judgment call on an approved list. Approved: Cap Undo cut is ghost (leftover / open the room stays primary); Home chat Send is ghost (the deck action stays); Trades Continue or Propose is the only primary (Accept and Load into builder are ghost).
- Native `<select>` is never used; `HubFilterMenu` is. Applies to Rules, DFS, Season, every page.

## Type
- Never below `--text-xs`. `--text-xs` must compute to at least 12px. Legal / compliance text is `--text-xs` or larger, muted color, and lives in the footer — not inline next to a heading.
- Eyebrow, H1, support sentence use the hero tokens on every page (`--experience-hero-heading`, `--experience-hero-pad`). Tools use the display H1 tokens. There is no third scale.

## Loading / empty
- Loading = skeleton with the final layout's dimensions. Never a sentence in place of a table.
- Empty = one shared empty-state (sentence + one CTA; `leagueBoardEmpty.js` / `HubEmptyState`). Not a paragraph, a button, and a footnote with three different gaps.

## When you find a violation on one page
- Fix the primitive (the shared CSS class or component), not the page. Then grep every consumer and run the audit on each. A page-scoped override of a shared primitive is a failing review.
